"Derek Ray" wrote:

> nethack.alt.org is probably our best universal,
> centralized source for any sort of data analysis
> regarding Nethack games

Well, no. It is a place to play that most people
find _after_, sometimes _long after_ finding
NetHack, so you probably are not, in general, seeing
naive players learning how to ascend, pretty much
the inference of the original query.

What you want for some data analysis like this is
the logs of some big university nethack host, where
the NetHack game is usually the players' _first_
encounter with NetHack and for a while, only access
to NetHack.

That has a bit of a problem the other way, that the
players may well leave before their first ascension,
but since we're looking for "best class" with the
implication "easiest class for a naive player", at
least it is sampling the right end of the playing
experince spectrum. I don't think the NAO logs do
that.

That doesn't make nattering over the NAO logs any
less fun, it just makes conclusions drawn using them
quite questionable.

